### The three upstream attribution obligations

All three upstreams are MIT, and MIT imposes the same three obligations on every
derivative of each of them. The Android and Windows ports wrote them out in their
own notices; the wording below is what they required, and it applies to all
three:

1. **Keep the licence text and this notice.** Ship the MIT text — the root
   `LICENSE` — and this `NOTICE` with every distribution, and keep the copyright
   lines restated in the table above.
2. **State the origin.** Credit the source in the product's about page, its
   documentation or its release page. The upstreams' own suggested wording is
   "Based on Jev Chat Assistant
   (https://github.com/jev-chat/jev-chat-jarvis)" for the first, "Integrated
   from jev-chat-windows
   (https://github.com/jev-chat/jev-chat-windows)" for the second, and the
   pinned commit above for the third. This `NOTICE` is that statement for this
   repository.
3. **Do not imply endorsement.** The upstream names, the "Jev 聊天助手" name and
   the upstream domains must not be used to imply that the upstream authors
